Aerie-Purpose: Move the address pill, Back, Forward, Reload and the rest of the toolbar into the Aerie sidebar, take the toolbar row away from the top of the window, and make the sidebar's top row the window's drag handle.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (browser_view.cc, vertical_tab_strip_region_view.*, layout/browser_view_tabbed_layout_impl.cc), chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar (toolbar_view.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #215 (items 1 and 2 of the rest of #177). All the work is in the overlay, chrome/browser/ui/views/aerie_sidebar
(AerieSidebarView::AdoptToolbar, AerieSidebarTopRow); these hooks only call it.

- browser_view.cc: right after the toolbar made its buttons (ToolbarView::Init, in AddedToWidget), a sidebar window hands
  the toolbar's views to the sidebar: the real LocationBarView (the address pill), Back, Forward and Reload (found by
  view id), and the toolbar itself, which keeps the extensions, profile and menu buttons and goes to the sidebar's bottom
  bar. Where the frame draws the window controls on the trailing side (Linux with the custom frame) the sidebar draws its
  own three and the frame's become invisible with Helium's SetCaptionButtonsOpacity. A leading exclusion (the macOS
  traffic lights) becomes an inset of the top row.
- vertical_tab_strip_region_view.*: forwards to the sidebar view; the empty part of the top row counts as the window
  caption in IsPositionInWindowCaption (the same hook Helium's top container uses). The sidebar answers before Helium's
  hidden bottom container, which would otherwise claim the whole column.
- browser_view_tabbed_layout_impl.cc: the toolbar is no longer a child of the top container, which the layout already
  handles (IsParentedTo), so the toolbar row is gone. The one change is the top of the collapsed column, which used to
  start under the toolbar and now starts at 0.
- toolbar_view.cc: the toolbar's own "collapse tabs" button stays hidden in the sidebar layout, because the top row has
  the toggle.

